# tests/fixtures/MANIFEST — the CLOSED inventory of tracked test FIXTURES.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. tests/no-rigs.test.sh was built on two different
# ideas at once. Under tests/lib/ it was a CLOSED ALLOW-LIST — a path is
# allowed only if a MANIFEST row declares it — and that half held against
# every attack a fresh adversarial tester threw at it. Under tests/fixtures/
# it was an OPEN DENY-LIST with exactly one refusal (mode 100755), and that
# half fell to the first push: the tester copied 120 real rig files out of
# lcars-dev/tests/drives/ into tests/fixtures/drives-archive/, stripped the
# exec bits, `git add -f`, and the gate printed the clean-tree tally. A rig
# script at mode 644 runs perfectly under `bash`, and the RECORDED .json and
# .log artefacts that were the actual bulk of the original 109 MB are inert
# data that an exec-bit rule can never reach.
#
# So tests/fixtures/ is now closed the same way tests/lib/ is: this file is
# the allow-list, and any tracked path under tests/fixtures/ without a row
# here is refused. A new fixture FAILS the build until someone adds a row.
# That friction is the same feature it is next door — the inventory can only
# grow deliberately, and "it's just data" stops being a way in.
#
# COLUMNS:  <git-index-mode> <path>
#
# The mode is checked, not just the path, so a symlink (120000) or an
# executable (100755) planted at a declared path is still refused. Fixtures
# are inert DATA by contract, so every row is 100644 and a 100755 anywhere
# under tests/fixtures/ is refused outright as `executable-fixture` before
# this list is even consulted.
#
# Paths may not contain spaces or newlines.

